			<item>
				<title>Data, Distributed Systems &amp; Security Quick Reference</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/self-review/quick-reference/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/self-review/quick-reference/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;kafka-production-defaults&#34;&gt;Kafka production defaults&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#kafka-production-defaults&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;table-wrap&#34; tabindex=&#34;0&#34; role=&#34;region&#34; aria-label=&#34;Table&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Setting&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Value&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;replication.factor&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;3 (across 3 AZs, rack-aware)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;min.insync.replicas&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;acks&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;all&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;enable.idempotence&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;unclean.leader.election.enable&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;compression.type&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;zstd&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;lz4&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;linger.ms&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;batch.size&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;5–20 ms / 64–256 KB&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;enable.auto.commit&lt;/code&gt; (business consumers)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt;; commit after processing&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;group.protocol&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;consumer&lt;/code&gt; (KIP-848)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;isolation.level&lt;/code&gt; (downstream of transactions)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;code&gt;read_committed&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Controllers&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;3 dedicated KRaft controllers&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;delivery-semantics&#34;&gt;Delivery semantics&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#delivery-semantics&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;table-wrap&#34; tabindex=&#34;0&#34; role=&#34;region&#34; aria-label=&#34;Table&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Need&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Use&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Loss acceptable&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;At-most-once&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Business events&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At-least-once + idempotent consumer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Kafka → process → Kafka&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Exactly-once (transactions / &lt;code&gt;exactly_once_v2&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;DB state + event&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Transactional outbox + CDC&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;API retries&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Idempotency-Key&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;which-pattern&#34;&gt;Which pattern?&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#which-pattern&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;table-wrap&#34; tabindex=&#34;0&#34; role=&#34;region&#34; aria-label=&#34;Table&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Problem&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Pattern&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;State change must emit an event reliably&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Outbox + CDC&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Duplicates&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Idempotent consumer / inbox&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Multi-service business transaction&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Saga (orchestrated for long flows)&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Reserve then commit&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;TCC / authorise–capture&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Different read and write shapes&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;CQRS&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Full history and audit&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Event sourcing&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Queue of independent jobs&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Kafka share group&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Ordered stream per entity&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Consumer group, keyed by entity&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Real-time aggregates and alerts&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Flink / Kafka Streams with event time&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;consistency-cheat-sheet&#34;&gt;Consistency cheat sheet&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#consistency-cheat-sheet&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;table-wrap&#34; tabindex=&#34;0&#34; role=&#34;region&#34; aria-label=&#34;Table&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Term&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;One-liner&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Linearizable&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Behaves like one copy, in real-time order&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Causal&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Causes are seen before effects&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Read-your-writes&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;You see your own updates&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Eventual&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Replicas converge when writes stop&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;CAP&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Under a partition: C or A&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;PACELC&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Else: latency or consistency&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Quorum&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;R + W &amp;gt; N&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Raft&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Majority commit; 3 or 5 nodes&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;table-formats-and-catalogs&#34;&gt;Table formats and catalogs&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#table-formats-and-catalogs&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;table-wrap&#34; tabindex=&#34;0&#34; role=&#34;region&#34; aria-label=&#34;Table&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;table&gt;&#xA;  &lt;thead&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Iceberg&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Delta&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;      &lt;th&gt;Hudi&lt;/th&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/thead&gt;&#xA;  &lt;tbody&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Strength&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Engine-neutral, REST catalog&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Spark/Databricks&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Upserts, incremental&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;    &lt;tr&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Catalogs&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Polaris, Unity, Glue/S3 Tables, Nessie&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Unity&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;      &lt;td&gt;Hive/Glue&lt;/td&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/tr&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/tbody&gt;&#xA;&lt;/table&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Iceberg v3: deletion vectors · row lineage · VARIANT · geo types · ns timestamps · defaults.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>About this handbook</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/about/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/about/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;purpose&#34;&gt;Purpose&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#purpose&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;Data, Distributed Systems &amp;amp; Cybersecurity Knowledge Hub&lt;/strong&gt; explains event streaming, distributed data consistency, data platforms and security architecture simply, with diagrams and flows. It is written for architects, senior engineers, data engineers and security engineers, especially those working in financial services. It is a companion to the &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/design-patterns-hub/&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Java &amp;amp; Software Architecture Knowledge Hub&lt;/a&gt;, the &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/enterprise-ai/&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Enterprise AI &amp;amp; Agentic AI Knowledge Hub&lt;/a&gt; and the &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/cloud-native/&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;&gt;Cloud Native &amp;amp; Platform Engineering Knowledge Hub&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Glossary</title>
				<link>https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/glossary/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/glossary/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Definitions are deliberately short. Follow the links for the full explanations.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;ac&#34;&gt;A–C&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#ac&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;dl&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABAC (attribute-based access control)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Access decisions from attributes of the user, the data and the context. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/data-platforms/data-security-and-privacy/&#34;&gt;Data security&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At-least-once delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Messages are never lost but may be duplicated. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/streaming/kafka-producers-and-consumers/&#34;&gt;Producers and consumers&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCBS 239&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Basel principles for risk data aggregation and reporting. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/data-platforms/data-governance/&#34;&gt;Data governance&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BOLA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Broken object-level authorisation, the top API security risk. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/security/security-architecture/&#34;&gt;Security architecture&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CAP theorem&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Under a network partition, choose consistency or availability. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/distributed/consistency-and-consensus/&#34;&gt;Consistency&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CDC (change data capture)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Streaming database changes from the transaction log. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/distributed/outbox-cdc-idempotency/&#34;&gt;Outbox and CDC&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CDE (cardholder data environment)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Systems that store, process or transmit card data, and so fall in PCI DSS scope. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/security/fintech-regulations/&#34;&gt;FinTech regulations&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensating transaction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;A business action that semantically undoes an earlier saga step. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/distributed/saga-pattern/&#34;&gt;Saga&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consumer group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Kafka consumers sharing partitions, one owner per partition. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/streaming/kafka-architecture/&#34;&gt;Kafka architecture&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CQRS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Separate models for commands (writes) and queries (reads). See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/distributed/cqrs-and-event-sourcing/&#34;&gt;CQRS and event sourcing&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Crypto-shredding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Making data unreadable by deleting its encryption key. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/data-platforms/data-security-and-privacy/&#34;&gt;Data security&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;/dl&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;di&#34;&gt;D–I&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#di&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;dl&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data contract&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;A producer–consumer agreement covering schema, semantics, quality, SLOs and ownership. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/streaming/schemas-and-event-contracts/&#34;&gt;Schemas and contracts&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data mesh&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Domain-owned data products on a self-serve platform with federated governance. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/data-platforms/data-platform-architecture/&#34;&gt;Data platforms&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DORA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;The EU Digital Operational Resilience Act for financial entities, applicable since January 2025. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/security/fintech-regulations/&#34;&gt;FinTech regulations&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DPDP Act&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;India&amp;rsquo;s Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023, with Rules notified in 2025. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/security/fintech-regulations/&#34;&gt;FinTech regulations&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Envelope encryption&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Data encrypted with a data key, and the data key encrypted with a master key in a KMS or HSM. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/data-platforms/data-security-and-privacy/&#34;&gt;Data security&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Event sourcing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Storing state as an append-only sequence of events. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/distributed/cqrs-and-event-sourcing/&#34;&gt;CQRS and event sourcing&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excessive agency&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;An AI system with more tools, permissions or autonomy than it needs. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/security/ai-security/&#34;&gt;AI security&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FAPI 2.0&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;OpenID Foundation security profile for financial-grade APIs. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/security/security-architecture/&#34;&gt;Security architecture&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Iceberg&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;An open table format adding ACID, schema evolution and time travel to files. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/data-platforms/data-platform-architecture/&#34;&gt;Data platforms&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Idempotency&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;An operation that has the same effect whether applied once or many times. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/distributed/outbox-cdc-idempotency/&#34;&gt;Outbox and idempotency&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ISR (in-sync replicas)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Kafka replicas caught up with the partition leader. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/streaming/kafka-architecture/&#34;&gt;Kafka architecture&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;/dl&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;kp&#34;&gt;K–P&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#kp&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;dl&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KRaft&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Kafka&amp;rsquo;s built-in Raft metadata quorum, replacing ZooKeeper since 4.0. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/streaming/kafka-architecture/&#34;&gt;Kafka architecture&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lakehouse&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Open table formats on object storage, queried by many engines under one catalog. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/data-platforms/data-platform-architecture/&#34;&gt;Data platforms&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lineage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;The record of where data came from and how it was transformed. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/data-platforms/data-governance/&#34;&gt;Data governance&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;LINDDUN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;A privacy threat-modelling method. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/security/threat-modelling/&#34;&gt;Threat modelling&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Linearizability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;The strongest single-object consistency: behaves like one copy in real-time order. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/distributed/consistency-and-consensus/&#34;&gt;Consistency&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Medallion architecture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Bronze (raw), silver (conformed) and gold (product) data layers. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/data-platforms/data-platform-architecture/&#34;&gt;Data platforms&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MITRE ATLAS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;A knowledge base of adversarial techniques against AI systems. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/security/ai-security/&#34;&gt;AI security&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Outbox pattern&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Writing state and event in one local transaction, and relaying the event later. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/distributed/outbox-cdc-idempotency/&#34;&gt;Outbox&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PACELC&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Partition: availability or consistency; else: latency or consistency. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/distributed/consistency-and-consensus/&#34;&gt;Consistency&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PCI DSS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;The security standard for cardholder data; v4.0.1 is current. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/security/fintech-regulations/&#34;&gt;FinTech regulations&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Post-quantum cryptography (PQC)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Algorithms resistant to quantum attacks (ML-KEM, ML-DSA, SLH-DSA). See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/security/security-architecture/&#34;&gt;Security architecture&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prompt injection&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Instructions in input or content that manipulate an LLM. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/security/ai-security/&#34;&gt;AI security&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;/dl&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;rz&#34;&gt;R–Z&lt;a class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34; href=&#34;#rz&#34; aria-label=&#34;Link to this section&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;dl&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Raft&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;A consensus protocol using leader election and majority log replication. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/distributed/consistency-and-consensus/&#34;&gt;Consistency&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Saga&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;A sequence of local transactions with compensations. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/distributed/saga-pattern/&#34;&gt;Saga&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SBOM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;A software bill of materials: an inventory of components. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/security/security-architecture/&#34;&gt;Security architecture&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SCA (strong customer authentication)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Two of knowledge, possession and inherence, required by PSD2. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/security/fintech-regulations/&#34;&gt;FinTech regulations&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Schema registry&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;A service that stores schema versions and enforces compatibility. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/streaming/schemas-and-event-contracts/&#34;&gt;Schemas and contracts&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Share group&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Queue-style Kafka consumption with per-record acknowledgement (KIP-932). See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/streaming/kafka-architecture/&#34;&gt;Kafka architecture&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SLSA&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Supply-chain Levels for Software Artifacts: build integrity and provenance. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/security/security-architecture/&#34;&gt;Security architecture&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;STRIDE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Spoofing, Tampering, Repudiation, Information disclosure, Denial of service, Elevation of privilege. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/security/threat-modelling/&#34;&gt;Threat modelling&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TCC (Try–Confirm–Cancel)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Reserve resources, then confirm or cancel them. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/distributed/distributed-transactions/&#34;&gt;Distributed transactions&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tokenisation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;Replacing sensitive values with random tokens mapped in a secure vault. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/data-platforms/data-security-and-privacy/&#34;&gt;Data security&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Watermark&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;A stream processor&amp;rsquo;s estimate of event-time progress, used to close windows. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/streaming/stream-processing/&#34;&gt;Stream processing&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;dt&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zero trust&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/dt&gt;&#xA;&lt;dd&gt;No implicit trust from network location; verify every request. See &lt;a href=&#34;https://samirsahoo.github.io/data-security/security/security-architecture/&#34;&gt;Security architecture&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/dd&gt;&#xA;&lt;/dl&gt;</description>
			</item>
